1
00:04:57,692 --> 00:05:03,692
Maestro is a drama, romance, music film directed by Bradley Cooper.

2
00:09:55,384 --> 00:10:01,384
A towering and fearless love story chronicling the lifelong relationship
between Leonard Bernstein and Felicia Montealegre Cohn Bernstein.

3
00:14:53,076 --> 00:14:59,076
A love letter to life and art, Maestro at its core is an
emotionally epic portrayal of family and love.

4
00:19:50,769 --> 00:19:56,769
Felicia Montealegre, played by Carey Mulligan.

5
00:24:48,461 --> 00:24:54,461
Leonard Bernstein, played by Bradley Cooper.

6
00:29:46,153 --> 00:29:52,153
David Oppenheim, played by Matt Bomer.

7
00:34:43,846 --> 00:34:49,846
Bruno Zirato, played by Vincenzo Amato.

8
00:39:41,538 --> 00:39:47,538
Isaac, played by Greg Hildreth.

9
00:44:39,230 --> 00:44:45,230
Jerry Robbins, played by Michael Urie.

10
00:49:36,923 --> 00:49:42,923
Maestro is a 2023 American biographical romantic drama film that centers on the relationship
between American composer Leonard Bernstein and his wife Felicia Montealegre.

11
00:54:34,615 --> 00:54:40,615
It was directed by Bradley Cooper, from a screenplay he wrote with Josh Singer.

12
00:59:32,307 --> 00:59:38,307
It was produced by Cooper, Martin Scorsese, Steven Spielberg,
Kristie Macosko Krieger, Fred Berner, and Amy Durning.

13
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
The film stars Carey Mulligan as Montealegre alongside Cooper as Bernstein.

14
01:09:27,692 --> 01:09:33,692
Matt Bomer, Maya Hawke, and Sarah Silverman appear in supporting roles.

15
01:14:25,384 --> 01:14:31,384
Plans for a Leonard Bernstein biopic began in 2008, but languished in
development hell for nearly a decade at Paramount Pictures.

16
01:19:23,076 --> 01:19:29,076
At various points both Martin Scorsese and Steven Spielberg were attached to direct, but
both eventually dropped out but remained on the project as producers.

17
01:24:20,769 --> 01:24:26,769
Cooper, who had already signed on to star in 2017, was then named as director following an early screening
of his directorial debut A Star Is Born (2018), and he rewrote Singer's original script.

18
01:29:18,461 --> 01:29:24,461
The rest of the cast joined between 2020 and 2023, and filming took place between May and October
2022, in Los Angeles, Massachusetts, Bernstein's home in Connecticut, and England.

19
01:34:16,153 --> 01:34:22,153
Maestro premiered at the 80th Venice International Film Festival on
September 2, 2023, where it was nominated for the Golden Lion.

20
01:39:13,846 --> 01:39:19,846
The film received a limited theatrical release on November 22,
2023, before being released on Netflix on December 20.

21
01:44:11,538 --> 01:44:17,538
It received generally positive reviews from critics, with praise given to the direction and the
performances, especially those of Cooper and Mulligan, but criticism of the writing and presentation.

22
01:49:09,230 --> 01:49:15,230
The film was named one of the top 10 of 2023 by the National
Board of Review and the American Film Institute.

23
01:54:06,923 --> 01:54:12,923
It received seven Academy Award nominations, including Best Picture, Best Actor (Cooper), and Best Actress (Mulligan), as
well as nominations for seven BAFTA Awards, four Golden Globe Awards, and two Screen Actors Guild Awards.

24
01:59:04,615 --> 01:59:10,615
The film explores themes of husband wife relationship, show
business, conductor, marriage, biography.

25
02:04:02,307 --> 02:04:08,307
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking.
